ng is not without risks. Three concerns dominate discussions on Xiaohongshu and in academic commentary."}]]}],["$","h3","282",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Risk 1: Resume Homogenization"}]]}],["$","p","284",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"If thousands of graduates use the same AI to optimize their resumes, the result is predictable: "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"homogenization"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". Career counselors at multiple universities have raised this concern. Li Hongfeng, director of career guidance at one participating university, told People's Daily: *\"We encourage students to treat AI suggestions as reference, not template. The system personalizes based on individual experience, but if everyone follows the same structural formula, differentiation disappears.\"*"}]]}],["$","h3","286",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Risk 2: Over-Reliance and Authenticity Erosion"}]]}],["$","p","288",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Some users report practicing so extensively with AI coaches that they struggle to adapt when real human interviewers deviate from predicted question patterns. The \"scripted\" feeling can backfire. Several Xiaohongshu posts describe interviewers explicitly saying, *\"Your answers feel very polished—can you tell me what you really think?\"*"}]]}],["$","h3","290",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Risk 3: Data Privacy and Biometric Concerns"}]]}],["$","p","292",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Video-based interview analysis requires capturing and processing "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"facial biometric data"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". While government-backed platforms like Jiangsu 24365 operate under public-sector data governance rules, commercial platforms have less transparent data policies. The facial analysis data—micro-expressions, emotional responses, stress indicators—constitutes sensitive personal information that could theoretically be repurposed for other profiling applications."}]]}],["$","hr","294",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","296",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Global Implications: Why the World Should Watch"}]]}],["$","p","298",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"AI interview coaching in China is not merely a local curiosity. It offers several lessons with global relevance."}]]}],["$","h3","300",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The \"Utility-First\" AI Application Model"}]]}],["$","p","302",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Chinese AI companies have historically excelled at "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"utility-first applications"}],["$","span","2",{"children":"—tools that solve immediate, high-frequency problems rather than pursuing general intelligence research. AI interview coaching exemplifies this: it leverages existing LLM capabilities (question generation, text evaluation) and combines them with narrow-domain AI (speech recognition, facial analysis) to create a product with immediate economic value."}]]}],["$","p","304",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Western AI development has often prioritized "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"research breakthroughs"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" over "}],["$","strong","3",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"practical deployment"}],["$","span","4",{"children":". China's approach—while sometimes criticized as \"application-layer copying\"—produces tools that reach tens of millions of users rapidly."}]]}],["$","h3","306",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Platform-Ecosystem Integration Play"}]]}],["$","p","308",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Chinese platforms benefit from integration into "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"super-app ecosystems"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" (WeChat Mini Programs) and "}],["$","strong","3",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"government-university partnerships"}],["$","span","4",{"children":" that would be difficult to replicate in Western markets. A U.S. state government partnering with a private AI company to deploy interview coaching at scale would face procurement, privacy, and political hurdles that China's centralized system avoids."}]]}],["$","h3","310",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Export Potential"}]]}],["$","p","312",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Several platforms—particularly HeyGen for digital humans, and potentially OfferGoose or MianShiMao for interview coaching—have clear "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"export potential"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" for overseas Chinese students and international job markets. As China's AI application layer matures, we should expect more \"reverse innovation\"—products developed for the Chinese market that find global adoption."}]]}],["$","hr","314",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","316",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"What Users Are Saying"}]]}],["$","blockquote","321",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"\"完成了这次AI视频模拟面试，我可以根据系统生成的建议及时复盘，后续还能多次演练。\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"After completing this AI video simulated interview, I can review in real-time based on the system's feedback and practice multiple times afterward.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— Wang Liuyu, Zhejiang University Master's student, Finance major"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","325",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"\"像是给简历做了'手术'，观感上确实焕然一新了。\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"It was like giving my resume surgery—the visual impression completely changed.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span